            <div xml:id="d550">

                <pb facs="0613" n="601" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg601"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.91262/199: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-03-20T17:00:00+02:00">March 20, 1941—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1039. Hottelet visited today by Embassy representative who found him obviously
                    well and composed and without complaint as to conditions and treatment. He
                    wished his family and home office assured of his confidence that his case will
                    be settled soon and satisfactorily and he sends best greetings. Arrangements
                    made to provide him with reading matter and desired personal items. Hottelet was
                    reassured that Embassy is following case closely. Local United Press office
                    informed of visit.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
